{
 "slug": "inferir/testes-de-hipotese",
 "modulo": "inferir",
 "tipo": "nb",
 "titulo": "12. Estatística inferencial: testes de um, dois e três ou mais grupos",
 "nav": "12.4–12.7 Testes de hipótese",
 "sobretitulo": "Notebook mestre",
 "descricao": "As diferenças observadas são estatisticamente significativas? E o teste A/B?",
 "origem": {
  "material": "Notebook mestre",
  "trecho": "seção 12.4 a 12.7 (células 212 a 226)"
 },
 "html": "<h2 id=\"secao-12-4\">12.4 Um grupo contra um valor de referência</h2>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> \"a média do grupo é diferente de um valor-alvo/histórico?\"</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Teste t de uma amostra</strong>: o desvio padrão populacional é desconhecido (caso comum).</li>\n<li><strong>Teste Z</strong>: só quando o desvio padrão <strong>populacional</strong> é conhecido, o que é raro na prática. Para n grande, os resultados de t e Z convergem.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">valor_referencia = <span class=\"tk-num\">10</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">amostra = dados_teste[var_num]</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\">t_stat, p = stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">ttest_1samp</span>(amostra, popmean=valor_referencia)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Teste t (1 amostra): t = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>t_stat<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.3f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Teste Z (statsmodels), para amostras grandes</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\"><span class=\"tk-kw\">from</span> statsmodels.stats.weightstats <span class=\"tk-kw\">import</span> ztest</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\">z_stat, p_z = <span class=\"tk-fn\">ztest</span>(amostra, value=valor_referencia)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Teste Z            : Z = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>z_stat<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.3f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p_z<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">Teste t (1 amostra): t = 1.204, p = 0.2291\nTeste Z            : Z = 1.204, p = 0.2288</pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"secao-12-5\">12.5 Dois grupos</h2>\n<h3 id=\"independentes-teste-t-student-welch-e-mann-whitney\">Independentes: teste t (Student/Welch) e Mann-Whitney</h3>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">grupo_1 = df.loc[df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_binaria</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] == <span class=\"tk-num\">0</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">dropna</span>()</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">grupo_2 = df.loc[df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_binaria</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>] == <span class=\"tk-num\">1</span>, <span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_num_2</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>].<span class=\"tk-fn\">dropna</span>()</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Paramétrico: equal_var=True → Student | equal_var=False → Welch (recomendado como padrão)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\">t_stat, p_t = stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">ttest_ind</span>(grupo_1, grupo_2, equal_var=<span class=\"tk-kw\">False</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Teste t de Welch : t = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>t_stat<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.3f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p_t<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"7\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"8\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Não paramétrico: compara as distribuições (postos), não as médias</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"9\">u_stat, p_u = stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">mannwhitneyu</span>(grupo_1, grupo_2, alternative=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">two-sided</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"10\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Mann-Whitney     : U = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>u_stat<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.0f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p_u<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">Teste t de Welch : t = -6.150, p = 4.174e-09\nMann-Whitney     : U = 43168, p = 2.189e-21</pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"pareados-mesmas-unidades-medidas-duas-vezes\">Pareados (mesmas unidades medidas duas vezes)</h3>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">ttest_rel</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_antes</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_depois</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>])    <span class=\"tk-com\"># paramétrico</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">wilcoxon</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_antes</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_depois</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>])     <span class=\"tk-com\"># não paramétrico</span></span></code></pre></div><aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>O que observar</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><ul>\n<li><code>alternative='two-sided'</code> (padrão) testa \"diferente\". Use <code>'less'</code> ou <code>'greater'</code> apenas se a direção foi definida <strong>antes</strong> de ver os dados.</li>\n<li>Mann-Whitney com distribuições de formas diferentes testa diferenças de <strong>distribuição</strong>, não só de mediana. Reporte medianas junto com o resultado.</li>\n</ul></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"secao-12-6\">12.6 Três ou mais grupos</h2>\n<p><strong>Por que não fazer vários testes t?</strong> Cada teste tem 5% de chance de falso positivo, e esses erros se acumulam. A ANOVA e o Kruskal-Wallis testam todos os grupos de uma vez. O pós-teste corrige as comparações múltiplas.</p>\n<h3 id=\"parametrico-anova-e-anova-de-welch\">Paramétrico: ANOVA (e ANOVA de Welch)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Estatística <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>variância entre grupos</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>variância dentro dos grupos</mtext></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. Um F alto indica que os grupos diferem mais do que o esperado pelo acaso.</li>\n<li>A ANOVA diz <strong>se</strong> há diferença, mas não <strong>onde</strong>. Para isso, use o pós-teste.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">f_stat, p_anova = stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">f_oneway</span>(*grupos.<span class=\"tk-fn\">values</span>())                       <span class=\"tk-com\"># ANOVA clássica (variâncias iguais)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">f_w, p_welch = stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">f_oneway</span>(*grupos.<span class=\"tk-fn\">values</span>(), equal_var=<span class=\"tk-kw\">False</span>)         <span class=\"tk-com\"># ANOVA de Welch (scipy ≥ 1.15)</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">ANOVA one-way: F = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>f_stat<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.2f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p_anova<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">ANOVA Welch  : F = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>f_w<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.2f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p_welch<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">ANOVA one-way: F = 52.60, p = 2.348e-22\nANOVA Welch  : F = 46.03, p = 1.064e-18</pre></div>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Pós-teste de Tukey (após ANOVA significativa): quais pares diferem?</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\"><span class=\"tk-kw\">from</span> statsmodels.stats.multicomp <span class=\"tk-kw\">import</span> pairwise_tukeyhsd</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\">tukey = <span class=\"tk-fn\">pairwise_tukeyhsd</span>(endog=dados_teste[var_num], groups=dados_teste[var_cat], alpha=ALFA)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(tukey.<span class=\"tk-fn\">summary</span>())     <span class=\"tk-com\"># reject=True → diferença significativa entre o par</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"6\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># alternativa scipy: stats.tukey_hsd(*grupos.values())</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">Multiple Comparison of Means - Tukey HSD, FWER=0.05\n==================================================\ngroup1 group2 meandiff p-adj  lower  upper  reject\n--------------------------------------------------\n     A      B   3.0382    0.0 1.8674 4.2089   True\n     A      C   5.6507    0.0  4.292 7.0094   True\n     B      C   2.6125 0.0001 1.1284 4.0967   True\n--------------------------------------------------</pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"nao-parametrico-kruskal-wallis-dunn\">Não paramétrico: Kruskal-Wallis + Dunn</h3>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">h_stat, p_kw = stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">kruskal</span>(*grupos.<span class=\"tk-fn\">values</span>())</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Kruskal-Wallis: H = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>h_stat<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.2f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p_kw<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">Kruskal-Wallis: H = 114.70, p = 1.239e-25</pre></div>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># Pós-teste de Dunn (após Kruskal significativo), com correção para comparações múltiplas</span></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\"><span class=\"tk-kw\">import</span> scikit_posthocs <span class=\"tk-kw\">as</span> sp</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"></span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"4\">sp.<span class=\"tk-fn\">posthoc_dunn</span>(dados_teste, val_col=var_num, group_col=var_cat, p_adjust=<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">bonferroni</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>).<span class=\"tk-fn\">round</span>(<span class=\"tk-num\">4</span>)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"5\"><span class=\"tk-com\"># matriz de p-valores: célula &lt; α → o par difere</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><div aria-label=\"Saída em tabela\" class=\"tabela\" role=\"region\" tabindex=\"0\"><table class=\"tabela-dados\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"col\"></th>\n<th scope=\"col\">A</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">B</th>\n<th scope=\"col\">C</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">A</th>\n<td class=\"num\">1.00</td>\n<td class=\"num\">0.00</td>\n<td class=\"num\">0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">B</th>\n<td class=\"num\">0.00</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1.00</td>\n<td class=\"num\">0.00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th scope=\"row\">C</th>\n<td class=\"num\">0.00</td>\n<td class=\"num\">0.00</td>\n<td class=\"num\">1.00</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span>O que observar</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><ul>\n<li>Só aplique o pós-teste se o teste global (ANOVA ou Kruskal) for significativo.</li>\n<li>O pós-teste deve combinar com o teste global: <strong>Tukey</strong> após ANOVA com variâncias iguais, <strong>Games-Howell</strong> após ANOVA de Welch (Seção <a href=\"/inferir/efeito-e-automacao/#secao-12-11\">12.11</a>) e <strong>Dunn</strong> após Kruskal-Wallis.</li>\n<li><em>Two-way</em> ANOVA (dois fatores ao mesmo tempo) requer <code>statsmodels</code> (<code>ols</code> + <code>anova_lm</code>) ou <code>pingouin.anova(between=[fator_1, fator_2])</code>.</li>\n</ul></div></aside>\n<h2 id=\"secao-12-7\">12.7 Associação entre duas categóricas: qui-quadrado <span class=\"selo selo--complemento\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\" title=\"Técnica que não estava no material de estudo original\">Complemento</span></h2>\n<p><strong>Quando usar:</strong> \"a distribuição de uma categórica depende da outra?\" (Seção <a href=\"/explorar/analise-bivariada-e-multivariada/#secao-8-4\">8.4</a>).</p>\n<div class=\"codigo\" data-lang=\"python\"><div class=\"codigo__barra\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><span class=\"codigo__lang\">python</span><button class=\"codigo__copiar\" data-copiar=\"\" type=\"button\">Copiar</button></div><pre aria-label=\"Código python\" class=\"codigo__pre\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"1\">tabela = pd.<span class=\"tk-fn\">crosstab</span>(df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_cat</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>], df[<span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">coluna_binaria</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>])</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"2\">chi2, p_chi2, gl, esperado = stats.<span class=\"tk-fn\">chi2_contingency</span>(tabela)</span>\n<span class=\"ln\" data-n=\"3\"><span class=\"tk-bi\">print</span>(<span class=\"tk-kw\">f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span><span class=\"tk-str\">Qui-quadrado: χ² = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>chi2<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.2f</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, gl = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>gl<span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">, p = </span><span class=\"tk-str\">{</span>p_chi2<span class=\"tk-str\">:</span><span class=\"tk-str\">.4g</span><span class=\"tk-str\">}</span><span class=\"tk-str\">'</span>)</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"saida\" data-pagefind-ignore=\"\"><p class=\"saida__rotulo\">Saída</p><pre class=\"saida__texto\" tabindex=\"0\">Qui-quadrado: χ² = 8.70, gl = 3, p = 0.03354</pre></div>\n<aside class=\"callout callout--atencao\"><p class=\"callout__titulo callout__titulo--so-icone\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"icone\" fill=\"none\" focusable=\"false\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"2\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3\"></path><path d=\"M12 9v4\"></path><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"></path></svg><span class=\"sr-only\">Atenção</span></p><div class=\"callout__corpo\"><p>O teste exige frequências esperadas ≥ 5 na maioria das células (confira em <code>esperado</code>). Se não for o caso, agrupe categorias, ou use <code>stats.fisher_exact</code> em tabelas 2×2.</p></div></aside>\n",
